  'Drama Club: Inversion',
  'Fix theatrical lines using inversion and emphasis.',
  'grammar',
  'C1',
  'hard',
  'Choose the most natural advanced form for each stage cue.',
  '{"prompt":"Advanced inversion in a drama-club crisis","questions":[{"question":"Backstage, the director whispers: “_____ had the curtain risen when the smoke alarm screamed.”","options":["Hardly","Hard","Hardly never","Almost soft","Barely not","Seldom soft"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Hardly had + subject + past participle = “almost immediately after”."},{"question":"An understudy sighs: “_____ I known the mic was dead, I would have projected more.”","options":["Had","Have","Did","Would","Were having","Should"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Had + subject + past participle is inverted third conditional."},{"question":"Critique note: “Not only _____ she forget the cue, she also waved at the wrong balcony.”","options":["did","does","do","doing","has","was"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"After “not only” in mid-sentence emphasis, invert with did + base verb."},{"question":"Program insert: “Rarely _____ such a still, listening house.”","options":["have we seen","we have seen","we saw have","seen we have","we seeing have","have seen we"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Negative adverbial (rarely) triggers inversion: auxiliary + subject + past participle."},{"question":"Choose the cleft that spotlights the costume: “_____ the ripped cape that stole the scene.”","options":["It was","It were","There was","It be","That were","It being"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"It-cleft: It was + noun phrase + that/who…"},{"question":"Stage manager: “Were it not _____ your quick tip, I’d still be hunting the prop sword.”","options":["for","to","of","by","with","on"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Fixed formal pattern: were it not for + noun."},{"question":"Which line uses correct inversion for emphasis?","options":["Never have I been so nervous on opening night","Never I have been so nervous on opening night","I never have been so nervous never on opening night","Have never I been so nervous on opening night","Never been I have so nervous on opening night","I have never been so nervous never opening"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Never + auxiliary + subject + past participle."},{"question":"Reviewer: “So rare _____ this cast chemistry that tickets vanished overnight.”","options":["was","were","be","been","been","being"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"So + adjective + was/were + subject (inversion after so + adj)."},{"question":"Prompt card: “Only after the blackout _____ the audience gasp as one.”","options":["did","does","do","had do","was do","have"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Only after… triggers inversion with did + base verb in past narrative."},{"question":"Which is a correct “little” inversion?","options":["Little did they realise the understudy was the star","Little they did realise the understudy was the star","Little realise they did the understudy was the star","They little did realise understudy the star","Did little they realise the understudy star","Little they realise did the understudy was star"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Little did + subject + bare infinitive."},{"question":"Actor improvises: “_____ should the fire curtain drop, exit calmly stage left.”","options":["Should","Would","Might will","Can if","Must that","Shall not"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Should + subject = formal conditional (“if the curtain drops”)."},{"question":"Choose the best emphatic rewrite of “I realised the mistake only then.”","options":["Only then did I realise the mistake","Only then I did realise the mistake","Only then realised I did the mistake","Then only I realise did the mistake","Did only then I realise the mistake","Only I then did realise mistake the"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"Only then + did + subject + base verb."},{"question":"Which sentence correctly uses “no sooner…than”?","options":["No sooner had she entered than the spotlight found her","No sooner she had entered than the spotlight found her","No sooner had she entered when the spotlight found her","No sooner she entered that the spotlight found her","No sooner entered she had than spotlight found","No sooner than she had entered the spotlight found"],"correctIndex":0,"explanation":"No sooner + had + subject + past participle + than…"}]}'::jsonb,
